title: The Army
view-if: bruning_plot == "successful" and paramilitaries_timer == 0
frequency: 100
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/d_rose.jpg
tags: fighting_paramilitaries

= The Army

Military availability : [+ military_available +]%

Military loyalty : [+ reichswehr_loyalty : loyalty +]

- @concessions_menu: We can give concessions to the military to calm them down.
- @root: Perhaps another time
- @easy_discard

@concessions_menu

- @promise_spending: We promise the army to fund them once this is over.
- @spending_1: We allocate a part of their budget to placate them.
- @delegate_1: We can delegate some of our paramilitary suppression operations to the Reichswehr.
- @spending_2: We can allocate a large portion of our budget on militarizing the Reichswehr even further.
- @delegate_2: We can give up major positions on anti streetfighting operations.
- @martial_law: With our situation, if it is better that Germany be under martial law than the extremists.

@promise_spending
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.05; military_weariness -= 10
subtitle: A vague promise of future military funding. It buys us time, but at the cost of credibility.

@spending_1
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.1; budget -= 1; military_weariness -= 15
subtitle: A small part of the budget is reallocated to calm military leadership. -1 budget

@delegate_1
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.15; military_weariness -= 15
subtitle: We let the Reichswehr handle some suppression. This helps — but we lose some civilian oversight.

@spending_2
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.25; budget -=2; military_weariness -= 20
subtitle: A major boost to Reichswehr capabilities. Effective, but controversial. -2 budget

@delegate_2
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.3; military_weariness -= 20
subtitle: We relinquish full operational control in key cities. Short-term order at a cost.

@martial_law
on-arrival: reichswehr_loyalty += 0.4
choose-if: 1 == 2
unavailable-subtitle: not done
subtitle: Germany enters martial law. The streets are quieter — but so is civil liberty.